          %h3#nets_and_filters Nets and filters
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
            is a generalization of a sequence; the definitions above serve to define a
            %strong Cauchy net
            without any change, other than allowing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_i)_i
            to be a net. This is precisely the structure of a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+space"} Cauchy space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+filter"} proper filter
            whose
            %span.newWikiWord
              canonical net
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/canonical+net"} ?
            is Cauchy.
          %p
            Note that in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+space"} complete space
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequentially+complete"} sequentially complete
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}
            is complete.
          %p
            When
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"} Bill Lawvere
            idenitified Lawvere metric spaces with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
